        "description": "Send one explicitly authorized local regular file to an independently authorized current UART target using its existing ZMODEM controller. Requires current resource/target revisions and epoch. Prepare the receiver separately and explicitly release any MCP input lease before sending; never auto-runs rz, opens a port or preempts another transfer. remoteName is a single protocol filename; destination directory and overwrite behavior belong to the receiver. Identical operationId/arguments retry the original record. A skipped file (ZSKIP) is not delivered. Protocol completion, file confirmation, remote publication and content verification are separate facts. Current native safe local source is Windows-only, at most 64 MiB. The finite deadline depends on actual size and baud rate; impossible budgets fail before protocol output.",
